  "id": "COMPOUND:280 - PROTEIN:5966",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which bleomycin interacts with the Leukocyte common antigen, mediated through a series of molecular targets. Bleomycin is known to interact with NCI-H1838 and P2X purinoceptor 3, both of which are targets of Mollicellin N, which in turn targets the Leukocyte common antigen. This indicates that bleomycin may exert its effects through a pathway involving the purinoceptor system, potentially modulating cellular signaling in leukocytes. The presence of multiple independent pathways linking bleomycin to the Leukocyte common antigen suggests a robust, mechanistically supported interaction, possibly through the inhibition of signaling pathways or direct receptor engagement. The consistent scores across the three paths further reinforce the reliability of this relationship, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
